      "name": "Temporal Eddies",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "arcane",
        "illusion"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per 10 minutes\n\n---\nEffect The dragon Strides or Flies up to their Speed, leaving behind afterimages of their past and future selves in each space they move through. Until the end of the dragon's next turn, they can use any of these spaces as the origin of their Strikes, spells, and other abilities. Observers also perceive the dragon in all these spaces simultaneously and must succeed at a DC 15 Flat check to target the dragon or fail to affect it. A creature can take a concentrate action to attempt to identify the dragon's true location with a successful DC 40 Will save save.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "PT10M"
